mount_nfs3 -- mount an NFS version 3 export under FreeMiNT
==========================================================

mount_nfs3 is the companion utility of the nfs3.xfs file system driver
(sys/xfs/nfs3). It talks version 3 of the MOUNT protocol (RFC 1813,
appendix I) to the server's rpc.mountd, gets a file handle for the
exported directory and hands it to the kernel driver with a Dcntl().

It is a separate program from mount_nfs, the NFS version 2 utility, and
the two are not interchangeable:

  - MOUNT version 1 returns a fixed 32 byte file handle, version 3
    returns a variable sized one of up to 64 bytes. That alone makes the
    Dcntl() structure incompatible, which is why mount_nfs3 uses its own
    opcodes (NFS3_MOUNT/NFS3_UNMOUNT) and a version 3 NFS_MOUNT_INFO.
  - The version 3 reply also lists the authentication flavours the
    server accepts; `-v' prints them.
  - Version 3 uses the mountstat3 status codes instead of plain errno
    values, so the error messages are more precise.

Usage:

    mount_nfs3 [ -rvnf ] [ -o options ] host:/remotedir localdir
    mount_nfs3 -u [ -vn ] localdir

localdir has to be below u:\nfs3, which is where nfs3.xfs installs
itself. The directory is created by the driver.

    -r      mount read only (same as -o ro)
    -o tcp  pin NFS over TCP (also proto=tcp); by default TCP is tried
            first and UDP is used if the connection fails
    -o udp  pin NFS over UDP (also proto=udp)
    -o      comma separated list of options, see mount_nfs3.8
    -v      verbose
    -n      do not update \etc\mtab
    -f      fake: only update \etc\mtab, do not really mount
    -u      unmount

Examples:

    mount_nfs3 fileserver:/srv/atari u:\nfs3\atari
    mount_nfs3 -o ro,rsize=8192,timeo=20 fileserver:/pub u:\nfs3\pub
    mount_nfs3 -u u:\nfs3\atari

See sys/xfs/nfs3/README for the driver side and for what changed between
NFS version 2 and version 3.
